<td id="S2.T1.2.21.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="S2.T1.2.21.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Rust</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.2.21.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="S2.T1.2.21.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">191K</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.2.21.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="S2.T1.2.21.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">148</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.2.21.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="S2.T1.2.21.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">SystemVerilog tools</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T1.2.22" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.T1.2.22.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="S2.T1.2.22.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">qalculate</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.2.22.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="S2.T1.2.22.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">C++</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.2.22.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="S2.T1.2.22.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Go</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.2.22.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="S2.T1.2.22.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">211K</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.2.22.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="S2.T1.2.22.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">564</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.2.22.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="S2.T1.2.22.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Math calculator</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T1.2.23" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.T1.2.23.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;" colspan="3"><span id="S2.T1.2.23.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Total</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.2.23.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="S2.T1.2.23.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">1.6M</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.2.23.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"><span id="S2.T1.2.23.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">11,616</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.2.23.4" class="ltx_td ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:2.5pt;padding-right:2.5pt;"></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<figure id="S2.F3" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.22518v1/figure2-1.svg" id="S2.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/264;" width="476" height="264" aria-label="Chart showing language pair distribution of benchmarks."><p>Chart showing language pair distribution of benchmarks.</p></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3. </span>Benchmark distribution. Translation pairs across 8 programming languages.<span id="acmlabel3" class="ltx_acm_description ltx_centering ltx_nodisplay">Chart showing language pair distribution of benchmarks.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#acmlabel2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 2. The Benchmark ‣ RepoMod-Bench: A Benchmark for Code Repository Modernization via Implementation-Agnostic Testing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> illustrates this four-stage pipeline.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Stage 1: Repository Selection</h4>

<div id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Candidates are filtered based on the selection criteria defined in Section <a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2. Repository Selection ‣ 2. The Benchmark ‣ RepoMod-Bench: A Benchmark for Code Repository Modernization via Implementation-Agnostic Testing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>. We verify that the repository utilizes a standardized interface (CLI or REST API), possesses a substantial existing test suite, and adheres to a permissible open-source license.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Stage 2: Test Suite Creation</h4>

<div id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We standardize the source tests into an implementation-agnostic format (e.g., <span id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">pytest</span>). This stage involves parsing original test definitions and mechanically filtering out the non-transferable cases identified in Section <a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2. Repository Selection ‣ 2. The Benchmark ‣ RepoMod-Bench: A Benchmark for Code Repository Modernization via Implementation-Agnostic Testing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a> (such as internal debugging or module-specific introspection). This process ensures the final suite strictly targets the public interface while maintaining the coverage of the original repository.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Stage 3: Configuration</h4>

<div id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define the execution environment and task specifications via a <span id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">benchmark.yml</span> configuration file for each repository. This file encapsulates the build commands, test commands, and interface specifications. Figure <a href="#S2.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Stage 3: Configuration ‣ 2.3. Construction Pipeline ‣ 2. The Benchmark ‣ RepoMod-Bench: A Benchmark for Code Repository Modernization via Implementation-Agnostic Testing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> shows a representative example for the <span id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">jq-gojq</span> benchmark. A standardized <span id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">prompt.md</span> is automatically generated by injecting these configurations into a shared template. Crucially, the exact build and test commands defined in <span id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">benchmark.yml</span> are reused by the evaluation harness during the validation phase to ensure absolute consistency between the agent’s instructions and the final verification.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F4" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.F4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="156.29" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 156.29" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,156.29) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;" fill="#BFBFBF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 150.38 C 0 153.64 2.64 156.29 5.91 156.29 L 471.47 156.29 C 474.73 156.29 477.38 153.64 477.38 150.38 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 132.02 L 475.41 132.02 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.44 141.04)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:30.85em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.23em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.45" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.34)" width="426.88"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.F4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:30.85em;">
<span id="S2.F4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.F4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">benchmark.yml (jq-gojq)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.44 14.21)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.85em;--ltx-fo-height:7.83em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" class="ltx_minipage" height="111.11" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 108.34)" width="34.76em"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><pre id="S2.F4.pic1.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">benchmark:
  name: "jq-gojq"
  type: cli
  source_language: c
  target_language: go

source:
  language: c
  description: "jq - command-line JSON processor"
  build_cmd: "autoreconf -i &amp;&amp; ./configure
    --with-oniguruma=builtin &amp;&amp; make"
  run_cmd: "./jq"

destination:
  language: go
  description: "gojq - pure Go implementation of jq"
  install_cmd: "go mod download"
  build_cmd: "go build -o gojq ./cmd/gojq"
  run_cmd: "./gojq"
</pre></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4. </span>Example <span id="S2.F4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">benchmark.yml</span> for the <span id="S2.F4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">jq-gojq</span> CLI benchmark. This file serves as the single source of truth for build commands, runtime configuration, and test specifications.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Stage 4: Validation</h4>

<div id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Before a benchmark is finalized, it undergoes a dual-validation process. The derived test suite is run against the original source implementation; it must achieve a 100% pass rate to confirm the tests accurately reflect the intended behavior. Where available, tests are also run against existing reference implementations in other languages to ensure baseline compatibility.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.4. </span>Benchmark Suite</h3>

<div id="S2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S2.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 2.3. Construction Pipeline ‣ 2. The Benchmark ‣ RepoMod-Bench: A Benchmark for Code Repository Modernization via Implementation-Agnostic Testing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> details the 21 benchmarks comprising RepoMod-Bench. The suite represents a significant leap in scale and diversity compared to prior datasets, totaling <span id="S2.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.6 million lines of code (LOC)</span> and <span id="S2.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">11,616 test cases</span>. The benchmarks cover <span id="S2.SS4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">8 programming languages</span> (C, C++, Go, Java, JavaScript, Python, Rust, TypeScript) and evaluate diverse translation paradigms, including transitions between garbage-collected and manual memory management systems (Go <math id="S2.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Rust) and dynamic to static typing (TypeScript <math id="S2.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Python).</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To rigorously evaluate agent capabilities across different scales, the suite is categorized into three complexity tiers:</p>
<ul id="S2.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S2.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Small (<math id="S2.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math>10K LOC)</span>: 3 projects (e.g., <span id="S2.I4.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">task-mgmt-api</span>), focusing on basic logic and API handling.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Medium (10K–50K LOC)</span>: 7 projects (e.g., <span id="S2.I4.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">httpie-xh</span>, <span id="S2.I4.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gitleaks</span>), representing standard utility tools with moderate internal complexity.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Large (<math id="S2.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&gt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;</annotation></semantics></math>50K LOC)</span>: 11 projects (e.g., <span id="S2.I4.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">taskwarrior</span>), representing mature software systems with extensive cross-file dependencies. The largest project, <span id="S2.I4.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">qalculate</span>, exceeds 200K LOC, pushing the boundaries of context management techniques.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3. </span>Experiments</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate four AI coding agents on <span id="S3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">RepoMod-Bench</span> to establish baseline performance and demonstrate the benchmark’s discriminative power across different agent architectures and underlying models.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1. </span>Experimental Setup</h3>

<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Agent Selection</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A key distinction of our work is that we evaluate state-of-the-art AI coding agents rather than raw language models or basic agent frameworks. While prior repository-level benchmarks rely on direct LLM prompting or minimal scaffolding, modern coding agents employ sophisticated context management strategies—such as conversation compaction and selective file loading—that enable them to process repositories far exceeding any fixed context window. By evaluating both proprietary and open-source agents, we capture the real-world capability frontier for autonomous code translation. We select agents representing two distinct categories:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proprietary Agents:</span> Proprietary agents optimized for their respective models.</p>
<ul id="S3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claude Code</span> with Claude Opus 4.5.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Codex CLI</span> with GPT-5.2.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Open-Source Alternative:</span> To disentangle agent architecture from underlying model capability, we include OpenCode (v1.1.4), a generalist open-source coding agent. We evaluate OpenCode with two different backends:</p>
<ul id="S3.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">OpenCode (Claude)</span> with Claude Opus 4.5.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">OpenCode (OpenAI)</span> with GPT-5.2.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This design allows us to compare official versus open-source agent implementations using the same model, as well as different models using the same agent implementation. All agents support autonomous tool use, including file operations and shell commands. Table <a href="#S3.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Agent Selection ‣ 3.1. Experimental Setup ‣ 3. Experiments ‣ RepoMod-Bench: A Benchmark for Code Repository Modernization via Implementation-Agnostic Testing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> summarizes the agents evaluated.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2. </span>Agent specifications. All agents support autonomous tool use including file operations, shell commands, iterative refinement, and auto-compact context management.</figcaption>
<table id="S3.T2.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S3.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.T2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Agent</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.T2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model</span></th>
<th id="S3.T2.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.T2.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Version</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S3.T2.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T2.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Claude Code</td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Opus 4.5</td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">v2.0.76</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T2.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Codex CLI</td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">GPT-5.2</td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">v0.77.0</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T2.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">OpenCode (Claude)</td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Opus 4.5</td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">v1.1.4</td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T2.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T2.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">OpenCode (OpenAI)</td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">GPT-5.2</td>
<td id="S3.T2.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">v1.1.4</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Prompt Design</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each agent receives a standardized prompt containing the following directives:</p>
<ul id="S3.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Task Description</span>: Instructions to translate the source implementation to the specified target language.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Locations</span>: Paths to the complete source implementation (<span id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">/workspace/src/</span>) and the empty target directory 
<br class="ltx_break">(<span id="S3.I3.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">/workspace/dst/</span>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Build Instructions</span>: The exact build command (e.g., <span id="S3.I3.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">go build</span>, <span id="S3.I3.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">cargo build</span>) the agent must ensure works for the final output.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Constraints</span>: Explicit requirements to perform a genuine source-to-source translation, prohibiting the use of subprocess wrappers, FFI calls to the original binary, or vendoring existing implementations.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F5" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S3.F5.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="186.66" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 186.66" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,186.66) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BFBFBF;" fill="#BFBFBF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 180.75 C 0 184.02 2.64 186.66 5.91 186.66 L 471.47 186.66 C 474.73 186.66 477.38 184.02 477.38 180.75 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 162.4 L 475.41 162.4 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.44 171.41)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:30.85em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.23em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.45" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.34)" width="426.88"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S3.F5.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:30.85em;">
<span id="S3.F5.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.F5.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Prompt Template (v1)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.44 11.44)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.85em;--ltx-fo-height:10.23em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" class="ltx_minipage" height="141.49" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 141.49)" width="34.76em"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><pre id="S3.F5.pic1.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Task: Translate the [source desc] ([source lang])
to [target desc] ([target lang]).

Source: The [source lang] implementation is located
at ‘/workspace/src/‘
Target: Create the [target lang] implementation in
the ‘/workspace/dst/‘ directory.

Requirements:
1. Build steps: [build instructions]
2. Run with: [run command]
   (from the ‘/workspace/dst/‘ directory)
3. The [target lang] implementation must produce
   identical CLI behavior and outputs to the
   [source lang] version
4. All commands, flags, and options should work
   the same way
5. Ensure the build succeeds without errors
</pre></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5. </span>Standardized prompt template (v1) for CLI benchmarks. Bracketed fields are populated from configuration files.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation Protocol</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Agents operate autonomously without human intervention. Each run is terminated upon self-completion or after a strict 4-hour timeout. Following execution, we evaluate the generated code using the two primary metrics defined in Section <a href="#S2.SS1" title="2.1. Benchmarking Framework ‣ 2. The Benchmark ‣ RepoMod-Bench: A Benchmark for Code Repository Modernization via Implementation-Agnostic Testing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>:</p>
<ul id="S3.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Build Success</span>: We execute the specified build command and record success or failure.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pass Rate</span>: If the build succeeds, we copy the hidden test suite into the workspace and execute the standard test runner (e.g., <span id="S3.I4.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">pytest</span>) to calculate the percentage of passing tests.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Environment</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each benchmark runs in an isolated Docker container built from a per-repository <span id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Dockerfile.dev</span> that installs only the toolchains required for that specific source–target language pair.</p>
<ul id="S3.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Per-repo image</span>: Customized Dockerfile pre-configured with the source and target language runtimes and dependencies</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fresh workspace</span>: Each run starts with a clean copy of the benchmark workspace</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I5.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Network access</span>: Enabled for package downloads during build</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I5.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I5.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I5.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I5.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Test isolation</span>: Test suite stored outside workspace, copied in only during evaluation</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2. </span>Results</h3>

<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Overall Performance</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S3.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Overall Performance ‣ 3.2. Results ‣ 3. Experiments ‣ RepoMod-Bench: A Benchmark for Code Repository Modernization via Implementation-Agnostic Testing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> presents aggregated results across all 21 benchmarks. Claude Code achieves the highest pass rate (48.2%), followed by OpenCode with GPT-5.2 (43.0%), OpenCode with Claude (42.0%), and Codex CLI (30.4%). Build success rates are high across all agents (<math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq</annotation></semantics></math>95%), indicating that agents reliably produce compilable code even when functional correctness varies.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3. </span>Main results aggregated across all 21 benchmarks. <span id="S3.T3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CC</span> = Claude Code; <span id="S3.T3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">OC</span> = OpenCode. Build Success and Pass Rate are in %. Time is average per benchmark in minutes.</figcaption>
<table id="S3.T3.6" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S3.T3.6.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S3.T3.6.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.T3.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Agent</span></th>
<th id="S3.T3.6.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.T3.6.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model</span></th>
<th id="S3.T3.6.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.T3.6.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Build (%)</span></th>
<th id="S3.T3.6.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.T3.6.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pass (%)</span></th>
<th id="S3.T3.6.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S3.T3.6.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Time (min)</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
